# Compiler-toolchain experiment workspace (local-only; synthetic fixtures,
# per-machine toolchain digests and regenerable measurement dumps. The real
# working copy lives on the WSL ext4 side — this entry keeps an accidental
# Windows-side copy out of the public repo)
compiler-experiment/

# Remotion product-explainer video project (local-only; the rendered mp4 and its
# ~500MB of Remotion/Chrome dependencies do not belong in the service repo)
video/

# Native build outputs under compiler/. The sources there are tracked, the
# artefacts are not: they are per-machine (they embed the local toolchain's
# layout), they are large, and an .o or .so that reaches a public commit cannot
# be taken back out of the history. Listed BEFORE the directory exists on
# purpose — the ordering is the point, not the paths.
compiler/**/build/
compiler/**/out/
compiler/**/bin/
compiler/**/*.o
compiler/**/*.so
compiler/**/*.a
compiler/**/*.elf
# A linked executable has no extension, so the patterns above cannot name it.
# The three output directories are the convention that makes it nameable; the
# ELF-header check in scripts/check-packaging-invariants.mjs is what catches a
# binary written anywhere else, loudly, instead of letting it be committed.

# Measurement output under compiler/, listed for the same reason and in the same
# order — before anything can write one. The rule those sources are written
# against is that measurements live on the Linux filesystem and never here: a
# recorded run embeds the local toolchain's digests and the absolute path of the
# tree it read, so a committed one is machine-specific noise at best and the
# layout of somebody's disk at worst. Intermediate IR and linker maps are on the
# list because they are the bulky, regenerable half of the same measurement.
#
# Fixtures are deliberately NOT listed. A fixture that turns up here is a
# decision someone made against the rule, and it should be visible in a diff and
# argued about, not swallowed silently by this file.
compiler/**/_lab/
compiler/**/_results/
compiler/**/*.log
compiler/**/*.map
compiler/**/*.ll
compiler/**/*.bc

# Local-only maintenance tooling. Scripts here encode naming rules that this
# repository is not the right place to publish — a checker that lists what it
# forbids hands the list to anyone who reads it. They run before a push, not in
# CI; what CI enforces is in scripts/ and phrased in product terms.
scripts-local/

# Measurement dumpers for the visualisation experiment. They walk the b1-evasion
# attack corpus under security-experiment/ and emit per-mutation-family recovery
# counts, so they carry the same attack premises that keep that folder out of the
# public repo. Their inputs and outputs are all ignored paths (paper_data/,
# video/src/data/, security-experiment/), so they are not runnable here anyway.
scripts/viz-*.mjs
